commit 69002bc8620ed10a0ec4910afc7ab5c8210b3acd
Author: Ryan C Tufts <ryan@chirality.ai>
Date:   Thu Oct 8 05:55:29 2026 -0600

    piping(T3 B1 SQ G6): re-pins at M = 10.5 GiB, G-B's SF-1 bound, N-1/N-2/N-5, the B1 witnesses and challenge, E-12 (I104)
    
    - Profile: the GENERATED PROFILE block regenerated at C = 3 with RV112 N-5's adapter
      reservations priced (SP's parked CaseSlots and per-case counters in T11; the batch
      PrimitiveSource vector in T13): 247 atoms, three new InBuild. E_mov,max + R in-build
      9,800,676,166 B sparse / 9,859,807,510 B dense (0.8693 / 0.8745 M at M = 10.5 GiB).
    - G-B (RV112 SF-1): phase_caps().late reads T11 less one case's late capture,
      F_T11_LATE_CAPTURE / C; a law test checks every coefficient of the form is a multiple of C.
    - Law tests: const M and the threshold pin at 11,274,289,152 B; the 0.9 M margin pins as
      floor(0.9 M); TEXT_TEXT_DIAG_ENV, L_PUB, L_DIAGID, Text(err), D_env, PushCap(D_env) at C = 3;
      PINNED_RECORD; challenge_bounds_are_the_profile extended to CAP_BYTES and the N1 text.
      N-1: the runner's C_PLUS_ONE line is read from source and held to C + 1. N-2: a C = 3
      parked-slot test with text in the last parked slot alone.
    - Witnesses: one entry point per mode; W2b's replacement (b2_k1e3), W-C2 (and at R/64),
      W-C2 (A, C), c1, the three-case input (inside D1 by assess); RSS_TIME controls; a DEF-O
      report (NC-1). Shared inputs in tests/common/b1_sq_inputs.rs, pinned by I86's input hashes.
    - Challenge: CAP_BYTES 16 GiB; A1-S-1's bound (W1 work, a successor or an N1 notice, by
      E_mov,max; otherwise the W1 phase); one entry point per input, mode and route.
    - E-12: s11f's rule 8 now scans retained_product.rs (two integer accumulations listed).
    
    The registration (threshold_bytes) is not applied: until it is, 8 of the retained_memory::
    lib tests, which need the registered M, fail by design (registration.diff, for ROOT after R6b).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

